# Underrealm Lich and Chains of Mephistopheles, both Bot1's, both replace its draws outside the first of its draw step, and
# Bot1 orders them each time (CR 616.1). Its turn 3 draw for the turn is exempt from Chains and replaced by the Lich alone,
# which finds Ancestral Recall among the top three. Of the spell's three draws Bot1 has the Lich apply first to the first:
# a look at the top three, and the card it takes is put into its hand, not drawn (CR 121.5), so Chains has nothing to
# replace. For the second it has Chains apply first: it discards that Island and so draws - and the Lich, which has not had
# its opportunity, replaces that draw (CR 614.5). The third is the Lich's again. Bot1 ends with two Islands.

